agentic-code-reviewers v0.4.0 (cursor-sdk)

⚠️ **WARNING:** `syncVault` performs `git pull --rebase` and `git push` on the vault tree without acquiring the same `.memo.lock` used by `upsertRecord`, `appendEvent`, `forgetRecord`, and `runGc`. When `vaultGit.enabled` is true, a concurrent mutation can interleave with pull/rebase/push, producing lost commits, rebase conflicts, or a vault snapshot that omits in-flight markdown writes.

**Correção sugerida:**

```typescript
export function syncVault(vaultRoot: string = getVaultRoot()) {
  acquireVaultLockSync(vaultRoot);
  try {
    // existing pull/push body
  } finally {
    releaseVaultLockSync(vaultRoot);
  }
}
```

<details>
<summary>🔍 Detalhes da Análise IA</summary>

**Score:** 6/10 | **Ação dev:** fix-code

**Análise:**
1. Evidence: `withVaultLock` serializes mutations in store.ts/curator.ts; `syncVault` (vault.ts:336–377) calls git commands with no lock wrapper, while `commitVaultChange` explicitly uses `acquireVaultLockSync`. 2. Scenario: terminal A runs `memo upsert`; terminal B runs `memo sync` before the auto-commit finishes — rebase/pull rewrites tracked files while markdown/SQLite are mid-update. 3. Protection: vault.test.ts only exercises sync in isolation; no concurrent sync+upsert test. 4. Discards: assuming single-user CLI use was rejected because vault-git spec targets multi-machine sync (explicit parallelism).

**Caminhos analisados:** /src/vault.ts, /src/store.ts, /src/cli.ts, /.agents/specs/vault-git.spec.md
</details>

agentic-code-reviewers v0.4.0 (cursor-sdk)

⚠️ **WARNING:** `memo doctor --rebuild` calls `rebuildIndex` outside the vault file lock. `rebuildIndex` deletes and rebuilds the entire FTS table from disk while other handlers may be writing markdown and incrementally updating SQLite via `indexRecord`, so concurrent MCP/CLI mutations can yield a transiently incomplete or stale search index.

**Correção sugerida:**

```typescript
import { withVaultLock } from './vault.js';

if (options.rebuild) {
  try {
    const rebuildRes = await withVaultLock(vaultRoot, () => rebuildIndex(vaultRoot));
    indexedRecordsCount = rebuildRes.indexed;
    ftsHealthy = true;
    rebuilt = true;
  } catch (err: unknown) {
    // existing warning handling
  }
}
```

<details>
<summary>🔍 Detalhes da Análise IA</summary>

**Score:** 6/10 | **Ação dev:** fix-code

**Análise:**
1. Evidence: doctor.ts:181 invokes `rebuildIndex(vaultRoot)` with no `withVaultLock`; store.ts mutations and runGc wrap writes in `withVaultLock`; indexer.ts:428 rebuild clears and rescans atomically only at the SQL layer, not filesystem coordination. 2. Scenario: agent upserts a trap while developer runs `memo doctor --rebuild`; rebuild scans vault mid-write and the new trap is missing from FTS until another rebuild. 3. Protection: doctor.test.ts covers rebuild success path only, not overlap with upsert. 4. Discards: WAL mode alone was rejected because rebuild deletes all FTS rows and rescans files — filesystem interleaving remains unprotected.

**Caminhos analisados:** /src/doctor.ts, /src/importer.ts, /src/indexer.ts, /src/store.ts
</details>

